# Media

Real-time media helpers in pure LOGOS, identical on every tier. Today: an AIMD bitrate controller
for adapting a stream to the link it is sent over. Auto-imported on first reference.

## Note
An AIMD bitrate controller: under loss it backs off multiplicatively (scaled by loss), on a clean link it climbs additively toward capacity, capped at 90% of the link with an 8 kbps floor.

## To adaptRate (currentKbps: Int) and (linkKbps: Int) and (lossPct: Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable target be currentKbps.
    If lossPct is at least 2:
        Let mutable cut be lossPct * 4.
        If cut is greater than 80:
            Set cut to 80.
        Set target to (currentKbps * (100 - cut)) / 100.
    If lossPct is less than 2:
        Let headroom be linkKbps - currentKbps.
        If headroom is greater than 0:
            Let mutable step be headroom / 20.
            If step is less than 8:
                Set step to 8.
            Set target to currentKbps + step.
    Let cap be (linkKbps * 9) / 10.
    If target is greater than cap:
        Set target to cap.
    If target is less than 8:
        Set target to 8.
    Return target.

## Note
Adjusts the jitter-buffer depth (ms): grows under high jitter or loss, shrinks on a clean low-jitter link, clamped to `[20, 500]`.

## To elasticBuffer (currentMs: Int) and (jitterMs: Int) and (lossPct: Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable target be currentMs.
    If jitterMs is greater than currentMs / 2:
        Set target to currentMs + jitterMs.
    If lossPct is at least 5:
        Set target to target + 40.
    If jitterMs is less than currentMs / 8:
        If lossPct is less than 1:
            Set target to currentMs - 20.
    If target is less than 20:
        Set target to 20.
    If target is greater than 500:
        Set target to 500.
    Return target.

## Note
Maps a continuous bitrate in kbps to a display label ("video-hd" down to "transcript") by threshold; a presentation hint only.

## To tierName (kbps: Int) -> Text:
    If kbps is at least 2000:
        Return "video-hd".
    If kbps is at least 800:
        Return "video-sd".
    If kbps is at least 300:
        Return "video-low".
    If kbps is at least 100:
        Return "avatar".
    If kbps is at least 30:
        Return "audio".
    Return "transcript".

## Note
Scalable (simulcast/SVC) layer selection: `cumulative` is the running bitrate at each quality layer; returns how many layers a receiver's `rateKbps` can sustain (no ceiling — a fat link clears all).

## To layersFor (rateKbps: Int) and (cumulative: Seq of Int) -> Int:
    Let mutable n be 0.
    Repeat for i from 1 to length of cumulative:
        If rateKbps is at least (item i of cumulative):
            Set n to i.
    Return n.
